.TH GOTO 1 "2025-05-29" "goto 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
goto \- directory shortcut manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B goto
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ name [ /subpath ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B goto
is a lightweight, POSIX\-compatible directory bookmark manager.
It lets you register named shortcuts to directories and instantly
jump to them with tab completion.
.PP
When invoked with a shortcut name,
.B goto
resolves the stored path and changes to that directory.
An optional subpath after the shortcut name navigates to a
subdirectory of the bookmarked location.
.PP
Shortcuts are stored in a plain\-text configuration file using a
simple pipe\-delimited format (name|path), one per line.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r " " \fIname\fR " [" \fIpath\fR "]"
Register or update a shortcut.
If
.I path
is omitted, the current working directory is used.
Relative paths are automatically resolved to absolute paths.
.TP
.BR \-d " " \fIname\fR ", " \-u " " \fIname\fR
Delete a shortcut.
.TP
.BR \-R " " \fIold\fR " " \fInew\fR
Rename a shortcut from
.I old
to
.IR new .
Fails if
.I new
already exists.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List all registered shortcuts.
Shortcuts pointing to nonexistent directories are marked as
.BR (missing) .
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cleanup
Remove all shortcuts whose target directories no longer exist.
.TP
.B \-\-export
Print all shortcuts to standard output in the config file format.
Useful for backing up or transferring shortcuts between machines.
.TP
.BI \-\-import " file"
Import shortcuts from
.IR file .
Entries with duplicate names overwrite existing shortcuts.
Invalid entries are skipped.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display the version number and exit.
.SH SHELL INTEGRATION
The
.B goto
binary outputs paths to standard output.
To enable the
.BR cd \-on\-resolve
behavior and tab completion, source the appropriate shell
integration file in your startup configuration:
.SS Bash and Zsh
.PP
Add to
.I ~/.bashrc
or
.IR ~/.zshrc :
.PP
.RS
.nf
source /usr/share/goto/goto.sh
.fi
.RE
.SS Fish
.PP
Install
.I goto.fish
to your Fish functions directory:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cp /usr/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/goto.fish \\
   ~/.config/fish/functions/goto.fish
.fi
.RE
.PP
Or, if installed via a package manager, Fish integration is
loaded automatically.
.SH SUBPATH NAVIGATION
A shortcut name can include a subpath separated by a forward slash:
.PP
.RS
.nf
goto myproject/src/lib
.fi
.RE
.PP
This resolves the
.B myproject
shortcut and appends
.B src/lib
to the resulting path.
Tab completion supports subpath navigation.
.SH SHORTCUT NAMES
Shortcut names may contain letters, digits, underscores, and hyphens.
Names are case\-sensitive.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:\-$HOME/.config}/goto/config
Shortcut database.
Plain\-text file with one entry per line in the format:
.br
.I name\fR|\fIpath
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
If set, the configuration directory is
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/goto/ .
Defaults to
.IR $HOME/.config/goto/ .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Operational error (shortcut not found, path does not exist).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (invalid arguments, missing required arguments).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Register the current directory as "work"
goto \-r work

# Register a specific path
goto \-r docs /home/user/Documents

# Jump to a shortcut
goto work

# Jump to a subdirectory of a shortcut
goto work/src/components

# List all shortcuts
goto \-l

# Remove broken shortcuts
goto \-\-cleanup

# Rename a shortcut
goto \-R work office

# Back up shortcuts to a file
goto \-\-export > ~/goto\-backup.txt

# Restore shortcuts from a backup
goto \-\-import ~/goto\-backup.txt
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cd (1),
.BR pushd (1)
